# TODO: Verification Plan for Protobuf PQ-Ratchet Serialization Functions

## Overview

This document describes the TODO plan for verifying the functions and constants
listed in [`doc/truong/pq_ratchet_functions.txt`](../truong/pq_ratchet_functions.txt),
which enumerates all fully qualified function and constant names from
`src/proto/pq_ratchet.rs` (Rust source). This file contains **no hand-written
code**: it consists entirely of a single `include!` directive that pulls in
the Rust code generated by `prost-build` from
[`src/proto/pq_ratchet.proto`](../../src/proto/pq_ratchet.proto).

All extractable functions are configured via
[`aeneas-config.yml`](../../aeneas-config.yml). The prost-generated
`prost::Message` trait implementations are declared **opaque** in
`aeneas-config.yml` (lines 50–52), so they are emitted as axioms in
`SrcTranslated/FunsExternal.lean` and their instance bodies are replaced
with `sorry` via post-extraction tweaks (lines 86–87). Functions gated behind
`#[cfg(not(feature = "extraction"))]` (e.g. `as_str_name`, `from_str_name`)
are not extracted because the Aeneas extraction uses `--features extraction`.

The type definitions from `pq_ratchet.proto` are extracted into
[`SrcTranslated/Types.lean`](../../SrcTranslated/Types.lean) as Lean 4
structures and inductives, and the non-opaque function bodies (Clone,
Default, PartialEq, Eq, Ord, enumeration helpers, TryFrom/From
conversions) are extracted into
[`SrcTranslated/Funs.lean`](../../SrcTranslated/Funs.lean).

There is currently **no Lean specification tree** for the `proto.pq_ratchet`
module. The protobuf types are used as parameters and return types by
other verified modules (notably the polynomial `into_pb`/`from_pb`
functions in [`Spqr/Specs/Encoding/Polynomial/`](../../Spqr/Specs/Encoding/Polynomial/))
but receive no dedicated verification.

