## 2. Skipped Functions and Reasons

### 2a. Opaque `prost::Message` Trait Methods (136 functions)

All `prost::Message` trait implementations (`encode_raw`, `merge_field`,
`encoded_len`, `clear`) for every message type in `pq_ratchet.proto`
are declared **opaque** in `aeneas-config.yml` (lines 50–52):

```yaml
opaque:
  - "spqr::proto::_::{impl prost::message::Message for _}"
  - "spqr::proto::_::_::{impl prost::message::Message for _}"
  - "spqr::proto::_::_::_::{impl prost::message::Message for _}"
```

As a result, Aeneas emits these functions as axioms in
`SrcTranslated/FunsExternal.lean` with no body to verify. The
corresponding `ProstMessageMessage` instance definitions in
`SrcTranslated/Funs.lean` are additionally replaced with `sorry` by
post-extraction tweaks (lines 86–87) because the struct-literal
instances exhibit self-referential field names that trigger Lean
termination errors.

| # | Functions | Why Skipped |
|---|-----------|-------------|
| F1–F136 | 34 types × {`encode_raw`, `merge_field`, `encoded_len`, `clear`} | Opaque axioms — no extracted body. Machine-generated protobuf wire-format code; verification would require modelling the prost encoding framework, which is out of scope. |

